Dear Hiring Team,

It is with great pleasure that I submit my candidacy for the Software Engineer, Agent Platform (New Grad) position with Netic. I bring over three years of professional experience building backend systems and production AI agents, along with a Master of Science in Computer Science from Pace University. Netic's mission to bring frontier AI to essential service industries is especially compelling to me because it pairs difficult systems engineering with immediate, tangible impact in the real economy.

At Sperse, I built the orchestration layer for a real-time multi-agent CRM platform using Python, FastAPI, LangGraph, and LangChain, routing requests among more than 40 specialized agents for over 10,000 users. I also shipped a TypeScript, Node, and React visual workflow platform backed by Temporal for durable execution, persisted state, retries, and failure recovery. That work maps directly to Netic's need for engineers who can route, sequence, and supervise multi-agent workflows while shipping full-stack agentic products. To validate changes before production, I extended agent harnesses with GitHub Actions CI/CD, OpenTelemetry trace-based eval loops, and guarded deployments that tested latency, accuracy, and safety.

My work also reflects the operational rigor required for agents that improve other agents. I built a FastMCP server exposing more than 160 validated backend actions and an OpenAI Codex review pipeline that automated 25–30 pull requests per week while preserving monitoring and human review checkpoints. At Qualitest, I orchestrated long-running distributed systems workflows with AWS Step Functions, improving retries, rollback paths, and error recovery across more than 100,000 weekly executions. Together with my Dark Factory project—a distributed coding-agent orchestrator with dependency-aware task DAGs, failure isolation, and resumable execution—these experiences prepare me to contribute to Agent Manager, execution harnesses, and customer-facing safeguards.

Netic's philosophy of living to build, obsessing over customers in each line of code, and refining execution with craftsmanship closely matches how I approach engineering. I would be excited to own outcomes, learn from a dedicated mentor, and help Netic build production-grade AI that lets essential service businesses grow on autopilot. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss the position and can be reached at #ph or #eml. Thank you for your time and consideration.

